<title>ITALY: Fiat shares buck weak trend on Milan bourse.</title>
<headline>Fiat shares buck weak trend on Milan bourse.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Italian industrial and car group Fiat rose around 0.8 percent in a generally weaker Italian stock market, with dealers citing investor interest from abroad.</p>
<p>Fiat shares, which peaked at 4,480 lire earlier, were 0.77 percent higher at 4,440 by 1015 GMT on turnover of more than five million shares.</p>
<p>Preference shares in one of the Agnelli family holdings Ifi rose two percent at 14,585, although dealers pointed out small orders were enough to move that stock.</p>
<p>The Mib30 index was 0.81 percent down at 14,987.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
